# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# awesome-lang-auth site — optional settings
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The site builds without any of these. To set one, copy this file to .env and
# rebuild:
#   cp .env.example .env && npm run build
#
# docusaurus.config.ts loads .env with dotenv at BUILD TIME, and the Docker
# build reads the same file (it is part of the build context), so a change
# needs a rebuild: `docker compose --profile <npm|traefik> up -d --build`.
# Never commit .env — it is listed in .gitignore.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Google Analytics 4 (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────

# GA4 Measurement ID — enables @docusaurus/plugin-google-gtag at build time.
# Obtain from Google Analytics → Admin → Data streams → Web → Measurement ID.
# Leave it unset to build without Google Analytics (the Umami script in
# docusaurus.config.ts is loaded either way).
# GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# ── Host port (docker compose only) ──────────────────────────────────────────

# Host port the container publishes (default 3000). docker compose reads it
# from this file for docker-compose.yml; the site itself does not.
# PORT=3000
